    "confidence": 0.6,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this dispute cannot be closed with a money order on the present record, so it goes to a human reviewer under POL-RD-10. Nothing is refunded and nothing further is collected — the SGD 26.73 already charged stands, and the SGD 11.00 contested is held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nWhat the record shows. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02826) is a METERED trip of 18.2 km billed at SGD 26.73, against a booked optimal of 14.0 km (EV-TRIP-02826). On those numbers the excess is 4.2 km, 30.0% of optimal, which would clear the POL-RD-01 gate (over 20% and over 0.8 km). Had the distance evidence held up, POL-RD-02 would recompute ((3.80 + 0.75 × 14.0 + 0.28 × 19.0) × 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee = 20.42, and refund 26.73 − 20.42 = 6.31, rounded up to SGD 6.35 — the figure the rider asks for. That refund cannot issue for the reason below.\n\nWhy no refund can issue. The GPS trace EV-GPS-02826 is impaired, weight_multiplier 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW: a 100-second sampling gap from 19:39:44 to 19:41:24 whose bounding fixes are 1.01 km apart. That breaches POL-RD-07(a) (over 90 seconds) and POL-RD-07(b) (over 500 m), so the trace is impaired for policy purposes as well as being flagged by the admissibility pre-pass — POL-GEN-02 says both things must be said, and they are. The 4.2 km excess is measured from that trace and from nothing else: the 18.2 km on the trip record is, by POL-RD-01's own terms, a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and may not be cited for the threshold test, and the billed 18.2 km on the fare ledger is likewise a copy. The driver's account, 'Navigation rerouted me', is a statement against interest that the vehicle was rerouted; I treat it as meeting POL-RD-07(ii)'s counterparty-statement limb, so the case is not escalated merely for want of corroboration. But a counterparty statement carries no weight_multiplier, so under POL-GEN-02(2) and the cap rule it neither raises nor lowers the confidence cap. The cap is therefore the impaired trace's 0.6, below the platform-wide escalation floor of 0.70, so POL-RD-10(1) requires escalation. Put the other way, if the driver's line were read as admitting no particular route, POL-RD-10(3) would compel the same escalation, because the impaired trace then has no independent corroboration of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) enumerates — the chat log is empty, there are no charged ERP gantries, and the trip record's distance is a copy.\n\nOther points, so both of you can see they were weighed. No rider-requested detour: the chat log (EV-CHAT-02826) is empty, so POL-RD-04 gives nothing. No amendment: the POL-RD-05 fields are null. Not pooled: vehicle_type is RYDE_X, so POL-RD-12 is not in play. Not an upfront fare: fare_model is METERED with no quoted fare, so POL-RD-11 does not run. No repeat-deviation pattern: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 287 completed trips, and the lifetime prior_deviation_flags (1), like rating, account age and cancellation rate on either profile, is context only under POL-GEN-01. No billing-integrity correction: no ERP gantries, no tolls, no airport surcharge, so POL-RD-09(4) has nothing to refund. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02826-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 is unavailable and the driver's traffic explanation carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13; but because the trace itself is impaired, POL-RD-13 does not convert this into a refund — POL-RD-07 governs. The driver's request for NO_ACTION is refused: POL-RD-07(iii) provides that an unproven claim resting on a broken trace is a data failure, and the outcome is escalation rather than a finding for the driver. POL-GEN-05 execution is moot while the case is escalated.\n\nDisclosure required by POL-GEN-02(3) and POL-RD-07: this ruling touches EV-GPS-02826 at weight 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW, and the impairment is why the ruling cannot be issued at the required confidence. What would resolve it: a record outside the single trace — an ERP gantry record with gantry name, time and cashcard reference placing the vehicle off the optimal corridor; a second, independent GPS export; or a corroborated amended-route figure. With that, the SGD 6.35 refund could be issued and the case would not need a human."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The one impairment cannot absorb the excess. It is a single 100.0 s sampling gap (19:39:44 to 19:41:24) whose bounding fixes are 1.01 km apart, on a trace with 94.5% coverage, 174 fixes and 30.3 minutes of running. POL-RD-07(i) requires the impaired stretch to be read as the straight line between its bounding fixes — the reading most favourable to the driver — and a 1.01 km stretch cannot account for a 4.2 km excess. The gap changes how one stretch is measured; it does not change whether a deviation exists.",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-02826 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "side": "RIDER"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The driver's explanation discharges nothing. Once the rider has shown a threshold-meeting excess, POL-RD-08 puts the burden on the driver to point to a specific artifact and a specific clause; 'Navigation rerouted me' names no advisory, no road and no evidence ID, so it carries no weight. POL-RD-13 requires such an assertion to be tested against the traffic_advisory and nothing else, and because no advisory identifier is cited, the missing advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction in it — so this is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. The driver is left with an unexplained 4.2 km.",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02826-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "side": "RIDER"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Even on the least favourable reading, the rider does not end up carrying the disputed charge. If the panel were to hold that the impaired trace has no independent corroboration, POL-RD-10(3) governs and the ruling is ESCALATE: terminal, no monetary outcome, and the disputed amount held rather than collected under POL-GEN-03. The primary case is a PARTIAL_REFUND of 6.35; the alternative holds the money. Neither leaves the rider paying for 4.2 km she did not travel.",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-02826 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "side": "RIDER"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and must measure an excess either from an unimpaired GPS trace or, where the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c), from an independent source named in POL-RD-07(ii). Limb (a) is met - TRP-02826 matches across the trip record, the trace and the fare breakdown - but limb (b) is not: the only excess figure in the bundle (4.2 km, 30.0%) is produced by the impaired trace itself, and the rider points to no POL-RD-07(ii) source. The burden never shifts to the driver, and the rider's claim is not sustained on this record.",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-02826 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "side": "DRIVER"
    },
    {
      "claim": "In the alternative - if the Judge were to establish a deviation despite the impaired trace - the measured excess of 4.2 km and 30.0% clears the POL-RD-01 establishment gate but sits below both material gates (50% and 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06(b) full-refund uplift is unavailable and the remedy is the POL-RD-02 arithmetic alone. On the fare breakdown's own figures that arithmetic gives charged_total 26.73 less a recomputed_fare of 20.42, i.e. 6.31 before rounding and 6.35 payable, which is well under 90% of the charged total. The 11.00 the rider contests is not supported by any line of the record and no FULL_REFUND is reached on any view.",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-02826 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "side": "DRIVER"
    }
  ]
}
